            <p>We're pleased to share the examples below as a snapshot of our approach to product storytelling, motion design and animation.</p>
            <p class="eyebrow">Quick note on the examples</p>
            <p>Many of these projects were designed to tell the larger product story, so they lean more heavily into narrative and brand than the specific product interactions outlined in this brief.</p>
            <p>For this assignment, we understand the distinction. The product needs to appear quickly and carry more of the story. But it also needs to be treated with <strong>purposeful motion, zooms, crops, annotations and transitions</strong> so it feels designed, <strong>not like a screen recording</strong>. While the objectives of these examples were different, they demonstrate the level of storytelling, animation and polish we would bring to that product-led approach.</p>
